========================================
BACKGROUND STORY – FENRIR
========================================

Fenrir was once an ordinary Chihuahua.
Alert, loud, and utterly convinced that he alone was responsible for defending
his territory from all airborne threats.

His owner was a gnome druid.
Why the druid chose to Awaken his dog was never explained.
Loneliness, curiosity, or simple amusement—only the result mattered.

Awakened, Fenrir gained speech and reason.
He did not gain humility.


The city was remarkably swift—some might say almost eager—to grant him commoner rights.
This enthusiasm, while initially suspicious, had a very simple explanation: commoners have to pay taxes. 
Sapience, intelligence, or an opinion on the matter was entirely optional.
Or to put it more simple - Fenrir had POaid his Scot and Lot (or Scutage in Fenrirs case, because standing on a wall donst make much sense in his case) - so he is a Citicen. If He is Sapient was never the question.
[OOC Clarification]  
Fenrir’s citizenship is not a joke rule.
Under medieval legal doctrine, any being that pays scot and lot is a recognized civic person.
Animals were historically subject to legal proceedings, so granting a dog with taxable income citizenship fits the period’s logic.
The exaggeration is comedic, but the legal principle is authentic.
[/OOC]


At present, Fenrir is employed at the city gate as a member of the City Guard, in the role of sniffing dog tasked with detecting forbidden chemicals. 
("K9" work)

